+# Matches a 16-digit credit card number written as four groups of four digits,
+# with no separator, with single spaces between the groups, or with single
+# hyphens between the groups. The separator must be the same throughout, so
+# "1234-5678 9012-3456" does not match. This checks the format only: it does
+# not check the issuer prefix or the Luhn check digit.
+credit_card = Regex(
+    r"(?:[0-9]{16}|[0-9]{4}(?: [0-9]{4}){3}|[0-9]{4}(?:-[0-9]{4}){3})"
+)
+
 # Matches any ISBN number. Note that this is not completely correct as not all
